{
  "_note": [
    "The app's own naming stock. Like tables_extra.json and appearance.json this is NOT a book",
    "transcription, so it may be widened freely; chargen.json and tables.json may not.",
    "",
    "Two things are being defended here, and they are different problems.",
    "",
    "BREADTH defends across seeds. Nothing a single run remembers can stop two Keepers, or one",
    "Keeper on two evenings, from drawing the same word — only the size of the pool can. The old",
    "town stock was 16 x 16 = 256, and the birthday bound puts the first repeat at about twenty",
    "draws, which is one campaign.",
    "",
    "FORM defends within a seed. A bigger word list alone yields 'The Ashes at Gallows Fork' and",
    "'The Judgment of the Hollow' — different words, one shape, and the pair still reads as the",
    "machine talking. So titles are built from templates, and Namer spends a form as readily as it",
    "spends a word. This is the fault that shipped: 'The Salt at Coffin Wells' and 'The Reckoning",
    "of the Wells' collided on the word AND on the shape.",
    "",
    "'spent' words below are the ones already on published work. They stay in the file so the",
    "history is legible, and Namer excludes them from first draw."
  ],

  "spent": ["Coffin", "Wells", "Salt", "Face", "Water", "Answers", "Reckoning"],

  "titleForms": [
